## 💡 More ways to keep your phone safe

- **Turn on Find Hub** (Google's Find My Device) so you can locate, lock or erase your phone.
- **Use a strong screen lock.** A password or a 6-digit PIN is much harder to guess than a 4-digit one.
- **Keep your phone updated** to get the latest security features.
- **Be careful in public places.** Many thefts happen while the phone is in your hand, for example while checking a map or taking a photo.

For step-by-step instructions, read our guide to the [top 5 Android settings to secure your phone against theft](/blog/top_five_settings).

---

## ℹ️ What happened to CrookCatcher's power menu blocking?

An earlier version of this article described an experimental CrookCatcher feature that blocked the power menu and notification shade on the lock screen. Because it couldn't work reliably across all Android phones, and Android and phone makers now offer better built-in protection, the feature has been discontinued. The settings above are the recommended way to protect your phone today.

